5 October 2026 adaptations: isolate the connection codec from the donor's
application, filesystem and account managers; validate BashKitten's existing
username syntax; add the QR quiet zone; exclude host code from client builds.
Retain TK2/version 2 field meanings, upstream age scrypt and Chisel wire/pipe
behavior. Dependency versions, complete pristine source and licenses are under
../../../auth and its upstreams.lock.json. No Chisel or age source patches.
The host adapter now rechecks active-carrier authorization and closes cancelled
handshakes. A private controller-pipe executable reuses that adapter, with no
public management listener or separate daemon lifecycle implementation.
OAuth authorization uses the protected browser's real persistent login session
and native interception of a query-mode PKCE callback, replacing the donor's
temporary login cookie jar/form parser. No replacement token issuer is added.
